<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96790" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στιγ-μᾰτίας</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στιγ-ίης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εω</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who bears tattoo-marks</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				4.2
			</span></i>; esp. <i>branded culprit</i> or <i>runaway slave</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Asius
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				159.14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				276.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				331
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Hermipp.
				63.19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				5.3.24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				47.10
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. οἰκέτης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ath.
					13.612c
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in Com.,
				<i>one whose property is marked</i> as mortgaged, <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				333
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> jocular
			nickname of Nicanor, the student of punctuation, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				20.12
			</span></i>, interpol. in <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νικάνωρ</span>
			.</div>
